INSERT INTO `incidents` VALUES ('INC-20261006-00001','The printer is not printing','Printer / Peripheral Issue',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-06 17:21:49','Office of the City Civil Registrar','The printer is not printing',NULL,'Maria Santos','Printer / Peripheral','1st floor','2026-10-07 12:28:45',4,'Low','Resolved','The printer located at the Office of the City Civil Registrar on the 1st floor is reported as not printing.','Potential causes include physical disconnection, power issues, depleted consumables, paper jams, or local print spooler and driver errors.','[{\"step\":\"Verify that the printer is powered on and the status light indicates it is ready.\",\"completed\":true},{\"step\":\"Check the printer display panel for any error messages, paper jams, or low ink/toner warnings.\",\"completed\":true},{\"step\":\"Ensure the USB or network cable is securely plugged into both the printer and the computer or wall outlet.\",\"completed\":true},{\"step\":\"Try restarting the printer by turning it off, waiting 10 seconds, and turning it back on.\",\"completed\":true}]','1. Check the print queue on the host computer or print server for any stuck, paused, or errored print jobs; clear the queue and restart the print spooler service if necessary to see if jobs begin processing. 2. Verify physical and network connectivity to the printer, including checking IP reachability via ping if it is a network printer or verifying port connections if locally attached, to confirm hardware communication.',2,1,'2026-10-06 17:24:16',4,'Paul Smith',0,'Printer driver was reinstalled, the print queue was cleared, and a test page was successfully printed.','2026-10-07 12:25:22'),('INC-20261007-00002','the printer power indicator has no light display while its plugin','Hardware / Power Issue',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-07 20:14:21','Office of the City Civil Registrar','the printer power indicator has no light display while its plugin',NULL,'Maria Santos','Printer / Peripheral','1st floor','2026-10-07 20:59:45',4,'Low','Resolved','The printer located in the Office of the City Civil Registrar on the 1st floor fails to power on, showing no light display on its power indicator even when plugged in.','The issue may be caused by a faulty wall outlet, a loose or damaged power cable, an inactive physical power switch on the printer, or an internal hardware failure such as a blown fuse or damaged power supply board.','[{\"step\":\"Verify that the power cable is firmly connected to both the printer and the wall outlet.\",\"completed\":true},{\"step\":\"Check if the printer has a physical power switch and ensure it is toggled to the \'On\' position.\",\"completed\":true},{\"step\":\"Try plugging the printer into a different, known-working wall outlet.\",\"completed\":true},{\"step\":\"Inspect the power cable for any visible physical damage, cuts, or bends.\",\"completed\":true}]','1. Verify the wall outlet power using a known working device or a voltage tester to ensure AC power is active at the 1st floor location. 2. Test the printer with a replacement power cable of the same specification to rule out a faulty cord. 3. Inspect the printer\'s power supply unit or internal fuse if power delivery fails despite verified outlet and cable integrity.',2,1,'2026-10-07 20:51:35',4,'Paul Smith',0,'printer is now working','2026-10-07 20:55:24'),('INC-20261007-00003','The desktop computer can\'t connect to the internet','Wireless Network Connectivity Issue',NULL,'Wi-Fi','2026-10-07 20:36:06','Office of the City Civil Registrar','The desktop computer can\'t connect to the internet','Desktop Computer','Maria Santos','Network Connectivity','1st floor',NULL,NULL,'Medium','Pending','A desktop computer in the Office of the City Civil Registrar on the 1st floor is unable to connect to the internet via Wi-Fi.','Potential causes include a disabled Wi-Fi adapter on the desktop, incorrect Wi-Fi credentials, weak wireless signal coverage on the 1st floor, or an issue with the local wireless access point.','[{\"step\":\"Verify that the Wi-Fi adapter on the desktop computer is turned on.\",\"completed\":false},{\"step\":\"Check if the correct Wi-Fi network is selected and try reconnecting.\",\"completed\":true},{\"step\":\"Verify if other nearby devices can connect to the same Wi-Fi network.\",\"completed\":true},{\"step\":\"Restart the desktop computer to refresh the network configuration.\",\"completed\":true}]','1. Verify the desktop computer\'s IP configuration using ipconfig in the command prompt to check if an IP address is correctly assigned by the DHCP server. 2. Test Wi-Fi hardware functionality by checking device manager for driver errors or disabling and re-enabling the wireless network adapter. 3. Check AP signal coverage and switchport status on the 1st floor to confirm the local wireless access point is operational and communicating with the core network.',2,1,'2026-10-13 09:54:18',4,'Paul Smith',NULL,NULL,NULL),('INC-20261009-DB1671','no internet connection','Wired Network Connectivity Issue','[\"Office of the City Civil Registrar\",\"2nd floor\",\"Network Connectivity\",\"Desktop Computer\",\"LAN\",\"no internet connection\",\"online services\"]','LAN','2026-10-09 14:12:42','Office of the City Civil Registrar','The desktop computer cannot access the internet through the wired LAN connection. The issue started today while the user was trying to access online services. Other applications that require an internet connection are also unable to connect','Desktop Computer','Maria Santos','Network Connectivity','2nd floor','2026-10-12 22:12:10',4,'High','Resolved','An employee at the Office of the City Civil Registrar located on the 2nd floor reported a Network Connectivity issue where a desktop computer has no internet connection over a wired LAN connection. The problem began today while attempting to access online services, and all other internet-dependent applications on the device are also failing to connect.',NULL,'Basic Self-Help:\n1. Verify that the Ethernet cable is securely plugged into both the back of the desktop computer and the wall data port, listening for a click and checking if link lights turn on. 2. Restart the desktop computer to refresh the local operating system network stack, and observe whether network connectivity is restored upon reboot. 3. Check the network icon in the taskbar to see if it shows a disconnected status, a warning symbol, or indicates that it is connected. 4. If the computer still cannot access the internet or online services, stop troubleshooting and report the issue to IT Support.','1. Verify physical Layer 1 connectivity by checking the switch port link and duplex status corresponding to the user\'s data drop on the 2nd floor. 2. Inspect the workstation\'s IP configuration (run ipconfig /all) to confirm valid DHCP assignment, subnet mask, default gateway, and DNS servers. 3. Test local gateway and external reachability using ping and traceroute commands. 4. If link or addressing issues persist, test the patch cable and wall jack with a network cable tester, and check switch logs for potential port security or VLAN misconfigurations. Note: Inquire if neighboring workstations in the Civil Registrar office are experiencing identical connectivity loss to rule out a localized switch/switch stack outage.\n[Employee checked self-help steps: 0,1,2,3]\n[IT checked troubleshooting steps: 0]',2,1,'2026-10-09 16:40:48',4,'Paul Smith',541,'Inspected the network connection and verified the workstation\'s IP configuration, default gateway, and DNS settings. Tested connectivity to the local gateway and external network using ping and traceroute. Checked the network cable, wall data port, and switch port status. The issue was resolved after correcting the network connection and verifying that the workstation could access the network and online services.','2026-10-12 13:10:51'),('INC-20261012-97D32B','Authentication Issue','Authentication Failure / Credential Input Error','[\"Office of the City Civil Registrar\",\"1st Floor\",\"Laptop\",\"Wi-Fi\",\"Authentication Issue\",\"Hardware Malfunction\",\"Wrong Credentials\"]','Wi-Fi','2026-10-12 13:11:49','Office of the City Civil Registrar','Wrong credentials input','Laptop','Maria Santos','Hardware Malfunction','1st','2026-10-16 04:38:05',4,'Critical','Resolved','An incident was reported by the Office of the City Civil Registrar located on the 1st floor involving a laptop connected via Wi-Fi. While logged under the Hardware Malfunction category with Authentication Issue as the affected service, the user specifically described the problem as wrong credentials input.',NULL,'Basic Self-Help:\n1. Check if the Caps Lock or Num Lock key is enabled on the laptop keyboard and toggle it off if needed. 2. Type your password slowly into a visible text field such as Notepad to verify that all keyboard keys are functioning properly and registering the correct characters. 3. Re-enter your username and password carefully into the authentication prompt to ensure accurate spelling and capitalization. 4. If the prompt continues to indicate wrong credentials, stop further attempts to prevent account lockout and contact IT Support for credential verification.','1. Review Active Directory, RADIUS, or Wi-Fi authentication controller logs to identify the exact cause of authentication failure (e.g., bad password, expired password, account locked, or missing certificates). 2. Test the laptop keyboard for hardware faults, such as stuck keys or incorrect character mapping. 3. Request clarification from the user regarding the specific service or network being accessed. 4. Reset the user credentials or re-enroll the Wi-Fi profile if policy requirements have changed.\n[Employee checked self-help steps: ]\n[IT checked troubleshooting steps: 0,1,2,3]',2,1,'2026-10-16 04:37:24',4,'Paul Smith',0,'fix','2026-10-16 04:37:54'),('INC-20261012-DA9CAC','server downtime','Physical Network Cabling / Access Point Connectivity','[\"Office of the City Civil Registrar\",\"2nd floor\",\"Server \\/ System Downtime\",\"Access Point\",\"LAN\",\"cable malfunction\",\"server downtime\"]','LAN','2026-10-12 12:03:53','Office of the City Civil Registrar','cable malfunction','Access Point','Maria Santos','Server / System Downtime','2nd floor','2026-10-12 12:23:22',4,'High','Resolved','An incident was reported by the Office of the City Civil Registrar located on the 2nd floor under the Server / System Downtime category, reporting server downtime affecting an Access Point connected via LAN due to a cable malfunction.',NULL,'Basic Self-Help:\n1. Visually inspect the network cable connected to your local equipment to see if it is securely seated in its port without forcing it. Observe if link indicator lights appear. 2. If the cable appears physically cut, frayed, or bent, do not touch or attempt to repair the wiring. Observe the condition and report it. 3. If there is still no network connection after checking that connections are seated, stop troubleshooting and report the issue to IT Support.','1. Perform a physical inspection and continuity test of the Ethernet drop and patch cables servicing the 2nd floor Access Point using a network cable tester. 2. Inspect the upstream switch port status for link state, speed/duplex mismatches, PoE delivery status, and CRC error counters. 3. Replace the suspect patch cable with a certified working cable to confirm if the fault is localized. 4. Clarify with the reporting office whether actual application servers are inaccessible or if the perceived server downtime is solely due to the Access Point losing network connectivity.\n[Employee checked self-help steps: 0,1,2]\n[IT checked troubleshooting steps: 0,1,2,3]',2,1,'2026-10-12 12:18:44',4,'Paul Smith',1,'naayos na','2026-10-12 12:22:00'),('INC-20261016-64753D','Cannot access office system','Security and Access Authentication Issue','[\"Office of the City Civil Registrar\",\"2nd floor\",\"Laptop\",\"Wi-Fi\",\"Access Issue\",\"Office System\"]','Wi-Fi','2026-10-16 06:20:40','Office of the City Civil Registrar','The user is unable to access the office system using a laptop connected to the office Wi-Fi. The system does not allow the user to log in or access the required records. Please analyze the possible causes and provide appropriate troubleshooting steps to restore access securely.','Laptop','Maria Santos','Security / Access Issue','2nd floor','2026-10-18 00:53:59',5,'High','Resolved','A user from the Office of the City Civil Registrar located on the 2nd floor reports being unable to access the office system on their laptop while connected to the office Wi-Fi. The user is currently unable to log in or access necessary office records, and they are seeking assistance to resolve this authentication or access restriction issue.',NULL,'Basic Self-Help:\n1. Restart your laptop and attempt to log in to the office system again. 2. Verify that you are connected to the correct office Wi-Fi network rather than a guest network. 3. Check if your keyboard\'s Caps Lock is off to ensure your password is entered correctly. 4. If access remains restricted after these steps, please document any specific error message displayed on the screen and contact the IT Department.','Verify user account status in Active Directory to rule out account lockout or password expiration. Perform a traceroute or ping test from the client\'s IP to the server to check for connectivity drops. Review system access logs for any rejected authentication attempts linked to the specific laptop\'s MAC address. Assess whether there have been recent updates to the firewall or access control lists (ACLs) affecting the 2nd-floor Wi-Fi subnet.\n[Employee checked self-help steps: 0,1,2,3]\n[IT checked troubleshooting steps: 0]',2,1,'2026-10-18 00:44:57',5,'Aljhon Reyes',6,'The user\'s access issue was investigated by verifying the laptop\'s Wi-Fi connection, checking the user account status, and reviewing authentication logs. The issue was resolved by correcting the account access configuration and confirming that the user could successfully log in to the office system and access the required records.','2026-10-18 00:47:59'),('INC-20261016-D934BE','Cannot access office system','Security / Access Issue','[\"Office of the City Civil Registrar\",\"Laptop\",\"Wi-Fi\",\"Access Issue\",\"Office System\"]','Wi-Fi','2026-10-16 06:08:32','Office of the City Civil Registrar','The user is unable to access the office system using a laptop connected to the office Wi-Fi. The system does not allow the user to log in or access the required records. Please analyze the possible causes and provide appropriate troubleshooting steps to restore access securely.','Laptop','Maria Santos','Security / Access Issue','2nd floor','2026-10-16 09:08:32',2,NULL,'Resolved','An employee from the Office of the City Civil Registrar located on the 2nd floor reports an inability to access the office system on their laptop while connected via Wi-Fi. The user is unable to log in or access necessary records.',NULL,'Basic Self-Help:\n1. Save any open work and restart your laptop to refresh network connections. 2. Verify that your keyboard Caps Lock is off and re-enter your credentials carefully. 3. Disconnect from the office Wi-Fi network and reconnect to see if the connection stabilizes. 4. If the error persists after two attempts, stop and contact IT Support immediately to avoid account lockout.','Review authentication logs for the specific user account to identify failed login attempts or account lockouts. Verify network connectivity between the 2nd-floor Wi-Fi access point and the application server. Check if the server-side access control list or firewall has restricted the device IP address. Conduct a test connection using an administrative account to isolate whether the issue is user-specific or system-wide.\n[Employee checked self-help steps: 0,1,2,3]',2,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('INC-20261017-231CE4','Email Sending Failure','Email Sending Failure','[\"Budget Office\",\"1st Floor\",\"Email\",\"Desktop\",\"LAN\",\"Outbox\"]','LAN','2026-10-18 00:55:02','Office of the City Budget Officer','The employee is unable to send emails using the office email application on their desktop computer. Outgoing messages remain stuck in the Outbox, and no confirmation of successful delivery is received. The computer is connected to the office network through LAN. Please investigate the email application settings, outgoing mail server connection, and network connectivity to identify the cause of the issue.','Desktop Computer','Hans Harvey Lascano','Email / Communication','1st floor','2026-10-18 01:05:13',5,'Medium','Resolved','An employee at the Office of the City Budget Officer, located on the 1st floor, is reporting an email sending failure on their desktop computer connected via LAN. The user states that outgoing messages are stuck in the Outbox and never receive delivery confirmation.',NULL,'Basic Self-Help:\n1. Save any work in the email application and close the program completely. 2. Re-open the email application and try to send a simple text-only test email without attachments. 3. Check if other internet-based applications, such as a web browser, are loading pages correctly to confirm basic network access. 4. If the test email remains in the Outbox, restart your computer and try again. 5. If the issue persists, do not attempt to modify server settings and contact IT Support for further assistance.','1. Verify network connectivity on the affected machine by performing a ping test to the mail server. 2. Check the email client\'s outgoing server (SMTP) configuration and authentication settings for accuracy. 3. Inspect the email application logs for specific error codes or timeout events. 4. Check if a local firewall or security software is blocking the mail application\'s access to the outbound mail port. 5. Ensure the user\'s account has not exceeded mailbox storage quotas or daily sending limits.\n[Employee checked self-help steps: ]\n[IT manually checked troubleshooting steps: 0,1,2,3,4]',19,1,'2026-10-18 00:56:14',5,'Aljhon Reyes',5,'The email sending issue was resolved by verifying the LAN connection, checking the outgoing mail server (SMTP) settings, and confirming the user\'s email account status. A test email was successfully sent and received, confirming that email communication was restored.','2026-10-18 01:00:10'),('INC-20261017-95BF84','Records Management System Login Error','Application Authentication Failure','[\"City Budget Office\",\"Records Management System\",\"Login Error\",\"Authentication\",\"Desktop\",\"LAN\"]','LAN','2026-10-17 23:45:54','Office of the City Budget Officer','The user is unable to log in to the Records Management System using valid credentials. The system does not proceed to the dashboard after clicking the login button. The issue affects access to the application\'s records and services. Please investigate the login functionality and check for possible application or server errors.','Desktop Computer','Hans Lascano','Software / Application Error','1st floor','2026-10-17 17:45:54',19,NULL,'Resolved','An employee at the Office of the City Budget Officer, located on the 1st floor, reported a software error on their desktop computer connected via LAN. The user is unable to access the Records Management System despite using valid credentials, as the system fails to proceed to the dashboard after clicking the login button, preventing access to essential records and services.',NULL,'Basic Self-Help:\n1. Close the web browser completely and reopen it. 2. Clear the browser\'s cache and cookies. 3. Attempt to log in again using an Incognito or Private window. 4. If the issue persists, contact the IT Support office for further assistance.','Review server-side authentication logs for the Records Management System. Check for API endpoint connectivity issues or potential database locking at the time of the login attempt. Validate user account permissions and session token validity on the application server.\n[Employee checked self-help steps: 0,1,2,3]',19,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('INC-DEMO-0001','network connection drops during file uploads','Network Connectivity','[\"demo\",\"network-connectivity\"]','Wi-Fi','2023-06-08 11:13:00','City Administrator\'s Office','Synthetic training report: User reports intermittent connectivity while accessing shared office files. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Desktop Computer','Diana Castillo B.','Network Connectivity','Main office, 2nd floor',NULL,NULL,'Medium','Pending','Network connection drops during file uploads.',NULL,'1. Verify that your desktop computer\'s Wi-Fi connection indicator shows a stable signal in the Main office on the 2nd floor, and observe if the signal fluctuates when you attempt to upload files. 2. Save your current work locally, disconnect from the Wi-Fi network, wait 30 seconds, reconnect to the office Wi-Fi network, and then check if the connection remains stable during a small test upload. 3. If the connection drops again during file uploads, stop troubleshooting and contact IT Support with your observations.','1. Verify the wireless access point signal strength and client association logs for the desktop computer located in the City Administrator\'s Office on the 2nd floor to check for intermittent disconnections or interference. 2. Inspect the desktop computer\'s Wi-Fi network adapter driver version and power management settings to ensure the adapter is not throttling or dropping the connection under high upload load. 3. Perform continuous ping tests and throughput checks from a similar device on the same Wi-Fi segment to determine if the issue is isolated to the user\'s desktop or indicative of broader wireless channel saturation.',4822,0,'2023-06-08 12:13:00',4,'Paul Smith',NULL,NULL,NULL),('INC-DEMO-0002','printer produces faint or misaligned output','Hardware Malfunction','[\"demo\",\"hardware-malfunction\"]','LAN','2024-11-15 13:26:00','Office of the City Budget Officer','Synthetic training report: Printed forms are faint and require inspection of toner and alignment. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Printer','Teresa De la Cruz M.','Hardware Malfunction','Records room',NULL,NULL,'Medium','Pending','Printer produces faint or misaligned output.',NULL,'1. Check the physical printer display to see if there are any low toner or error warnings, and observe if a clear status message appears. 2. Print a test page directly from the printer menu to determine if the issue persists outside of the LAN connection, and observe the print quality. 3. If the print quality remains faint or misaligned, stop troubleshooting and contact IT Support for further assistance.','1. Verify the printer configuration and print density settings via the print server or local device management interface to check if toner conservation mode is enabled. 2. Inspect the physical print cartridge and rollers for toner depletion, debris, or wear that could cause faintness or misalignment. 3. Run printer calibration utilities to correct alignment issues and test output quality.',4859,0,'2024-11-15 14:26:00',5,'Aljhon Reyes',NULL,NULL,NULL),('INC-DEMO-0003','records application freezes while saving a form','Software / Application Error','[\"demo\",\"software-/-application-error\"]','LAN','2026-04-03 15:39:00','Office of the City Environment & Natural Resources Officer','Synthetic training report: Application becomes unresponsive during routine record updates. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Desktop Computer','Emilio Domingo X.','Software / Application Error','Conference room A',NULL,NULL,'Low','Pending','Records application freezes while saving a form.',NULL,'1. Wait a few moments to see if the application completes the save operation and recovers from the freeze. 2. If the application remains completely unresponsive, close the application window if possible or use Task Manager to end the application process. 3. Reopen the records application, log back in, and check if the record was saved or if it needs to be re-entered. 4. If the freezing persists every time you attempt to save, stop and contact IT Support for assistance.','1. Verify network connectivity and check switch port status for the LAN connection in Conference room A to rule out packet loss during the save action. 2. Review local event logs and application crash dumps on the desktop computer to identify any resource exhaustion or application fault signatures. 3. Check application server logs to determine if database locking, timeouts, or backend errors occurred concurrently with the user\'s save attempt.',4896,0,'2026-04-03 16:39:00',6,'Carlo Mendoza',NULL,NULL,NULL),('INC-DEMO-0004','email client repeatedly requests sign-in','Email / Communication','[\"demo\",\"email-/-communication\"]','Wi-Fi','2022-11-10 17:52:00','Office of the City Health Officer','Synthetic training report: Employee is prompted to authenticate again when opening the office mailbox. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Laptop','Victoria Flores I.','Email / Communication','Public service counter',NULL,NULL,'Medium','Pending','Email client repeatedly requests sign-in.',NULL,'1. Close the email client completely and reopen it to see if the sign-in prompt clears. 2. Verify that your laptop is actively connected to the Wi-Fi network and can load web pages. 3. Restart your laptop and attempt to open the email client again. 4. If the prompt persists, stop and contact IT Support for credential or client profile assistance.','1. Check if other users on the same network are experiencing similar authentication loops to isolate whether it is a network or client-side issue. 2. Verify the account status of the employee in the identity provider or mail server to ensure the account is not locked or requiring a password reset. 3. Inspect the email client profile on the laptop and clear cached credentials or recreate the mail profile if token caching is corrupted.',4933,0,'2022-11-10 18:52:00',7,'Ebin Garcia',NULL,NULL,NULL),('INC-DEMO-0005','shared records system responds slowly','Server / System Downtime','[\"demo\",\"server-/-system-downtime\"]','LAN','2024-04-17 10:05:00','Office of the City Legal Officer','Synthetic training report: Several staff members report delayed responses from the shared records application. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Desktop Computer','Gabriel Hernandez T.','Server / System Downtime','Annex, 1st floor',NULL,NULL,'Medium','Pending','Shared records system responds slowly.',NULL,'1. Close and restart the shared records application on your desktop computer, then check if the response time improves. 2. Restart your web browser or client application if you are accessing the system through a browser interface. 3. If the application continues to lag after a restart, stop troubleshooting and contact IT Support to report ongoing system slowness.','1. Check server resource utilization and application logs for the shared records system to determine if there is high CPU, memory, or database locking causing delays. 2. Verify network connectivity and switch port status on the LAN switch serving the Annex 1st floor to rule out packet loss or duplex mismatches. 3. Test direct access to the records server from an administrative diagnostic machine to isolate whether the issue is isolated to the client subnet or affects the entire service.',4970,0,'2024-04-17 11:05:00',8,'Pao Santos',NULL,NULL,NULL),('INC-DEMO-0006','account cannot open an assigned shared folder','Security / Access Issue','[\"demo\",\"security-/-access-issue\"]','LAN','2025-09-05 12:18:00','Office of the City Prosecutor','Synthetic training report: Access request needs verification against the employee’s current office responsibilities. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Desktop Computer','Amihan Mendoza E.','Security / Access Issue','Main office, 1st floor',NULL,NULL,'Low','Pending','Account cannot open an assigned shared folder.',NULL,'1. Verify that you are logged into your primary domain account correctly and restart your Desktop Computer. 2. Attempt to access the shared folder again and observe if an error message appears. 3. If access is still denied, stop troubleshooting and contact IT Support with the specific error message.','1. Verify the user account permissions and access control lists (ACLs) on the target shared folder to ensure the correct rights are assigned. 2. Confirm whether the user\'s current office responsibilities align with the requested folder access per department policy. 3. Check network connectivity and domain controller communication from the desktop computer to ensure group policy and authentication tokens are updating correctly.',5007,0,'2025-09-05 13:18:00',9,'Jampee Flores',NULL,NULL,NULL),('INC-DEMO-0007','laptop battery drains unusually quickly','Hardware Malfunction','[\"demo\",\"hardware-malfunction\"]','LAN','2022-04-12 14:31:00','Office of the City Veterinarian','Synthetic training report: Device battery life has declined during normal office use. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Laptop','Isabel Mercado P.','Hardware Malfunction','Main office, 2nd floor',NULL,NULL,'Medium','Pending','Laptop battery drains unusually quickly.',NULL,'1. Check the current battery health settings or battery usage monitor on your laptop to identify if a specific application is consuming excessive power and close it. Observe if the discharge rate slows down. 2. Disconnect any non-essential USB devices or peripherals connected to the laptop that might be drawing power, then observe if battery life improves. 3. Adjust your screen brightness to a lower level and enable power saver mode. If the battery still drains rapidly under light use or fails to hold a charge, stop and contact IT Support for hardware assessment.','1. Run a built-in battery diagnostic tool or generate a battery report (e.g., using powercfg /batteryreport on Windows) to check design capacity versus full charge capacity and review recent usage history. 2. Inspect power management settings, startup applications, and drivers to ensure there are no software anomalies causing excessive power draw. 3. If battery health metrics indicate significant degradation, arrange for physical inspection and replacement of the laptop battery.',5044,0,'2022-04-12 15:31:00',10,'Ken Bautista',NULL,NULL,NULL),('INC-DEMO-0008','wireless connection is unavailable in one meeting room','Network Connectivity','[\"demo\",\"network-connectivity\"]','Wi-Fi','2023-09-19 16:44:00','Business Permits & Licensing Office [BPLO]','Synthetic training report: Wi-Fi signal is weak in a single meeting room; nearby rooms are unaffected. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Tablet','Apolinario Ramos A.','Network Connectivity','Records room',NULL,NULL,'Medium','Pending','Wireless connection is unavailable in one meeting room.',NULL,'1. Move the tablet slightly within the meeting room to check if the weak Wi-Fi signal improves and observe if the wireless connection stabilizes. 2. Toggle the tablet\'s Wi-Fi off and back on to refresh the connection to the network and check if the affected service becomes available. 3. Restart the tablet completely if the connection remains unavailable, then verify if the Wi-Fi signal is detected. 4. If the wireless connection is still unavailable after trying these steps in the meeting room, stop and contact IT Support.','1. Verify the wireless access point coverage and signal strength in and around the specific meeting room to identify potential dead zones or physical interference. 2. Check the access point logs and client association metrics for the affected tablet to determine if authentication or signal degradation issues are occurring in that location.',5081,0,'2023-09-19 17:44:00',11,'KM Dela Cruz',NULL,NULL,NULL),('INC-DEMO-0009','network connection drops during file uploads','Network Connectivity','[\"demo\",\"network-connectivity\"]','Wi-Fi','2025-02-07 09:57:00','Transportation Development Regulatory Office [TDRO]','Synthetic training report: User reports intermittent connectivity while accessing shared office files. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Desktop Computer','Luningning Reyes L.','Network Connectivity','Conference room A',NULL,NULL,'Low','Pending','Network connection drops during file uploads.',NULL,'1. Verify that your desktop computer\'s Wi-Fi connection indicator shows a stable signal in the Main office on the 2nd floor, and observe if the signal fluctuates when you attempt to upload files. 2. Save your current work locally, disconnect from the Wi-Fi network, wait 30 seconds, reconnect to the office Wi-Fi network, and then check if the connection remains stable during a small test upload. 3. If the connection drops again during file uploads, stop troubleshooting and contact IT Support with your observations.','1. Verify the wireless access point signal strength and client association logs for the desktop computer located in the City Administrator\'s Office on the 2nd floor to check for intermittent disconnections or interference. 2. Inspect the desktop computer\'s Wi-Fi network adapter driver version and power management settings to ensure the adapter is not throttling or dropping the connection under high upload load. 3. Perform continuous ping tests and throughput checks from a similar device on the same Wi-Fi segment to determine if the issue is isolated to the user\'s desktop or indicative of broader wireless channel saturation.',5118,0,'2025-02-07 10:57:00',12,'Marvin Ramos',NULL,NULL,NULL),('INC-DEMO-0010','printer produces faint or misaligned output','Hardware Malfunction','[\"demo\",\"hardware-malfunction\"]','LAN','2026-07-14 11:10:00','Public Library and Information Center [PLIC]','Synthet