determine if the issue persists outside of the LAN connection, and observe the print quality. 3. If the print quality remains faint or misaligned, stop troubleshooting and contact IT Support for further assistance.','1. Verify the printer configuration and print density settings via the print server or local device management interface to check if toner conservation mode is enabled. 2. Inspect the physical print cartridge and rollers for toner depletion, debris, or wear that could cause faintness or misalignment. 3. Run printer calibration utilities to correct alignment issues and test output quality.',4943,0,NULL,13,'Michael Castillo',354,'Synthetic demo resolution: verified the affected device, applied the appropriate configuration or repair, and confirmed service with the reporter.','2024-11-05 11:42:00'),('INC-DEMO-0235','records application freezes while saving a form','Software / Application Error','[\"demo\",\"software-/-application-error\"]','LAN','2026-04-12 11:55:00','Public Affairs & Assistance Division[PAAD]','Synthetic training report: Application becomes unresponsive during routine record updates. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Desktop Computer','Tomas Hernandez D.','Software / Application Error','Main office, 2nd floor','2026-04-12 17:55:00',14,'Medium','Resolved','Records application freezes while saving a form.',NULL,'1. Wait a few moments to see if the application completes the save operation and recovers from the freeze. 2. If the application remains completely unresponsive, close the application window if possible or use Task Manager to end the application process. 3. Reopen the records application, log back in, and check if the record was saved or if it needs to be re-entered. 4. If the freezing persists every time you attempt to save, stop and contact IT Support for assistance.','1. Verify network connectivity and check switch port status for the LAN connection in Conference room A to rule out packet loss during the save action. 2. Review local event logs and application crash dumps on the desktop computer to identify any resource exhaustion or application fault signatures. 3. Check application server logs to determine if database locking, timeouts, or backend errors occurred concurrently with the user\'s save attempt.',4980,0,NULL,14,'Topher Villanueva',355,'Synthetic demo resolution: verified the affected device, applied the appropriate configuration or repair, and confirmed service with the reporter.','2026-04-12 13:55:00'),('INC-DEMO-0236','email client repeatedly requests sign-in','Email / Communication','[\"demo\",\"email-/-communication\"]','Wi-Fi','2022-11-19 13:08:00','City Tourism Office','Synthetic training report: Employee is prompted to authenticate again when opening the office mailbox. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Laptop','Felisa Mendoza O.','Email / Communication','Records room','2022-11-19 19:08:00',15,'Medium','Resolved','Email client repeatedly requests sign-in.',NULL,'1. Close the email client completely and reopen it to see if the sign-in prompt clears. 2. Verify that your laptop is actively connected to the Wi-Fi network and can load web pages. 3. Restart your laptop and attempt to open the email client again. 4. If the prompt persists, stop and contact IT Support for credential or client profile assistance.','1. Check if other users on the same network are experiencing similar authentication loops to isolate whether it is a network or client-side issue. 2. Verify the account status of the employee in the identity provider or mail server to ensure the account is not locked or requiring a password reset. 3. Inspect the email client profile on the laptop and clear cached credentials or recreate the mail profile if token caching is corrupted.',5017,0,NULL,15,'Willem Navarro',356,'Synthetic demo resolution: verified the affected device, applied the appropriate configuration or repair, and confirmed service with the reporter.','2022-11-19 15:08:00'),('INC-DEMO-0237','shared records system responds slowly','Server / System Downtime','[\"demo\",\"server-/-system-downtime\"]','LAN','2024-04-07 15:21:00','Public Employment Services Office [PESO]','Synthetic training report: Several staff members report delayed responses from the shared records application. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Desktop Computer','Zenaida Mercado Z.','Server / System Downtime','Conference room A','2024-04-07 21:21:00',16,'Low','Resolved','Shared records system responds slowly.',NULL,'1. Close and restart the shared records application on your desktop computer, then check if the response time improves. 2. Restart your web browser or client application if you are accessing the system through a browser interface. 3. If the application continues to lag after a restart, stop troubleshooting and contact IT Support to report ongoing system slowness.','1. Check server resource utilization and application logs for the shared records system to determine if there is high CPU, memory, or database locking causing delays. 2. Verify network connectivity and switch port status on the LAN switch serving the Annex 1st floor to rule out packet loss or duplex mismatches. 3. Test direct access to the records server from an administrative diagnostic machine to isolate whether the issue is isolated to the client subnet or affects the entire service.',5054,0,NULL,16,'Tops Aquino',357,'Synthetic demo resolution: verified the affected device, applied the appropriate configuration or repair, and confirmed service with the reporter.','2024-04-07 17:21:00'),('INC-DEMO-0238','account cannot open an assigned shared folder','Security / Access Issue','[\"demo\",\"security-/-access-issue\"]','LAN','2025-09-14 17:34:00','Sangguniang Panlungsod','Synthetic training report: Access request needs verification against the employee’s current office responsibilities. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Desktop Computer','Hannah Ramos K.','Security / Access Issue','Public service counter','2025-09-14 23:34:00',17,'Medium','Resolved','Account cannot open an assigned shared folder.',NULL,'1. Verify that you are logged into your primary domain account correctly and restart your Desktop Computer. 2. Attempt to access the shared folder again and observe if an error message appears. 3. If access is still denied, stop troubleshooting and contact IT Support with the specific error message.','1. Verify the user account permissions and access control lists (ACLs) on the target shared folder to ensure the correct rights are assigned. 2. Confirm whether the user\'s current office responsibilities align with the requested folder access per department policy. 3. Check network connectivity and domain controller communication from the desktop computer to ensure group policy and authentication tokens are updating correctly.',5091,0,NULL,17,'Mike Fernandez',358,'Synthetic demo resolution: verified the affected device, applied the appropriate configuration or repair, and confirmed service with the reporter.','2025-09-14 19:34:00'),('INC-DEMO-0239','laptop battery drains unusually quickly','Hardware Malfunction','[\"demo\",\"hardware-malfunction\"]','LAN','2022-04-02 10:47:00','City Administrator\'s Office','Synthetic training report: Device battery life has declined during normal office use. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Laptop','Andres Rivera V.','Hardware Malfunction','Annex, 1st floor','2022-04-02 16:47:00',18,'Medium','Resolved','Laptop battery drains unusually quickly.',NULL,'1. Check the current battery health settings or battery usage monitor on your laptop to identify if a specific application is consuming excessive power and close it. Observe if the discharge rate slows down. 2. Disconnect any non-essential USB devices or peripherals connected to the laptop that might be drawing power, then observe if battery life improves. 3. Adjust your screen brightness to a lower level and enable power saver mode. If the battery still drains rapidly under light use or fails to hold a charge, stop and contact IT Support for hardware assessment.','1. Run a built-in battery diagnostic tool or generate a battery report (e.g., using powercfg /batteryreport on Windows) to check design capacity versus full charge capacity and review recent usage history. 2. Inspect power management settings, startup applications, and drivers to ensure there are no software anomalies causing excessive power draw. 3. If battery health metrics indicate significant degradation, arrange for physical inspection and replacement of the laptop battery.',5128,0,NULL,18,'Ryan Morales',359,'Synthetic demo resolution: verified the affected device, applied the appropriate configuration or repair, and confirmed service with the reporter.','2022-04-02 12:47:00'),('INC-DEMO-0240','wireless connection is unavailable in one meeting room','Network Connectivity','[\"demo\",\"network-connectivity\"]','Wi-Fi','2023-09-09 12:00:00','Office of the City Budget Officer','Synthetic training report: Wi-Fi signal is weak in a single meeting room; nearby rooms are unaffected. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Tablet','Joaquin Santos G.','Network Connectivity','Main office, 1st floor','2023-09-09 18:00:00',1,'High','Resolved','Wireless connection is unavailable in one meeting room.',NULL,'1. Move the tablet slightly within the meeting room to check if the weak Wi-Fi signal improves and observe if the wireless connection stabilizes. 2. Toggle the tablet\'s Wi-Fi off and back on to refresh the connection to the network and check if the affected service becomes available. 3. Restart the tablet completely if the connection remains unavailable, then verify if the Wi-Fi signal is detected. 4. If the wireless connection is still unavailable after trying these steps in the meeting room, stop and contact IT Support.','1. Verify the wireless acce