1 16:38:00','Sangguniang Panlungsod','Synthetic training report: Access request needs verification against the employee’s current office responsibilities. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Desktop Computer','Carmela Aguilar Q.','Security / Access Issue','Records room','2026-05-11 22:38:00',9,'Medium','Resolved','Account cannot open an assigned shared folder.',NULL,'1. Verify that you are logged into your primary domain account correctly and restart your Desktop Computer. 2. Attempt to access the shared folder again and observe if an error message appears. 3. If access is still denied, stop troubleshooting and contact IT Support with the specific error message.','1. Verify the user account permissions and access control lists (ACLs) on the target shared folder to ensure the correct rights are assigned. 2. Confirm whether the user\'s current office responsibilities align with the requested folder access per department policy. 3. Check network connectivity and domain controller communication from the desktop computer to ensure group policy and authentication tokens are updating correctly.',5227,0,NULL,9,'Jampee Flores',325,'Synthetic demo resolution: verified the affected device, applied the appropriate configuration or repair, and confirmed service with the reporter.','2026-05-11 18:38:00'),('INC-DEMO-0567','laptop battery drains unusually quickly','Hardware Malfunction','[\"demo\",\"hardware-malfunction\"]','LAN','2022-12-18 09:51:00','City Administrator\'s Office','Synthetic training report: Device battery life has declined during normal office use. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Laptop','Nina Alcantara B.','Hardware Malfunction','Conference room A','2022-12-18 15:51:00',10,'Low','Resolved','Laptop battery drains unusually quickly.',NULL,'1. Check the current battery health settings or battery usage monitor on your laptop to identify if a specific application is consuming excessive power and close it. Observe if the discharge rate slows down. 2. Disconnect any non-essential USB devices or peripherals connected to the laptop that might be drawing power, then observe if battery life improves. 3. Adjust your screen brightness to a lower level and enable power saver mode. If the battery still drains rapidly under light use or fails to hold a charge, stop and contact IT Support for hardware assessment.','1. Run a built-in battery diagnostic tool or generate a battery report (e.g., using powercfg /batteryreport on Windows) to check design capacity versus full charge capacity and review recent usage history. 2. Inspect power management settings, startup applications, and drivers to ensure there are no software anomalies causing excessive power draw. 3. If battery health metrics indicate significant degradation, arrange for physical inspection and replacement of the laptop battery.',5264,0,NULL,10,'Ken Bautista',326,'Synthetic demo resolution: verified the affected device, applied the appropriate configuration or repair, and confirmed service with the reporter.','2022-12-18 11:51:00'),('INC-DEMO-0568','wireless connection is unavailable in one meeting room','Network Connectivity','[\"demo\",\"network-connectivity\"]','Wi-Fi','2024-05-06 11:04:00','Office of the City Market Administrator','Synthetic training report: Wi-Fi signal is weak in a single meeting room; nearby rooms are unaffected. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Tablet','Felisa Bautista G.','Network Connectivity','Public service counter','2024-05-06 17:04:00',11,'Medium','Resolved','Wireless connection is unavailable in one meeting room.',NULL,'1. Move the tablet slightly within the meeting room to check if the weak Wi-Fi signal improves and observe if the wireless connection stabilizes. 2. Toggle the tablet\'s Wi-Fi off and back on to refresh the connection to the network and check if the affected service becomes available. 3. Restart the tablet completely if the connection remains unavailable, then verify if the Wi-Fi signal is detected. 4. If the wireless connection is still unavailable after trying these steps in the meeting room, stop and contact IT Support.','1. Verify the wireless access point coverage and signal strength in and around the specific meeting room to identify potential dead zones or physical interference. 2. Check the access point logs and client association metrics for the affected tablet to determine if authentication or signal degradation issues are occurring in that location.',4801,0,NULL,11,'KM Dela Cruz',327,'Synthetic demo resolution: verified the affected device, applied the appropriate configuration or repair, and confirmed service with the reporter.','2024-05-06 13:04:00'),('INC-DEMO-0569','network connection drops during file uploads','Network Connectivity','[\"demo\",\"network-connectivity\"]','Wi-Fi','2025-10-13 13:17:00','Office of the City Social Welfare & Development Officer','Synthetic training report: User reports intermittent connectivity while accessing shared office files. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Desktop Computer','Zenaida Castillo R.','Network Connectivity','Annex, 1st floor','2025-10-13 19:17:00',12,'Medium','Resolved','Network connection drops during file uploads.',NULL,'1. Verify that your desktop computer\'s Wi-Fi connection indicator shows a stable signal in the Main office on the 2nd floor, and observe if the signal fluctuates when you attempt to upload files. 2. Save your current work locally, disconnect from the Wi-Fi network, wait 30 seconds, reconnect to the office Wi-Fi network, and then check if the connection remains stable during a small test upload. 3. If the connection drops again during file uploads, stop troubleshooting and contact IT Support with your observations.','1. Verify the wireless access point signal strength and client association logs for the desktop computer located in the City Administrator\'s Office on the 2nd floor to check for intermittent disconnections or interference. 2. Inspect the desktop computer\'s Wi-Fi network adapter driver version and power management settings to ensure the adapter is not throttling or dropping the connection under high upload load. 3. Perform continuous ping tests and throughput checks from a similar device on the same Wi-Fi segment to determine if the issue is isolated to the user\'s desktop or indicative of broader wireless channel saturation.',4838,0,NULL,12,'Marvin Ramos',328,'Synthetic demo resolution: verified the affected device, applied the appropriate configuration or repair, and confirmed service with the reporter.','2025-10-13 15:17:00'),('INC-DEMO-0570','printer produces faint or misaligned output','Hardware Malfunction','[\"demo\",\"hardware-malfunction\"]','LAN','2022-05-01 15:30:00','Office of the City Agriculturist','Synthetic training report: Printed forms are faint and require inspection of toner and alignment. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Printer','Hannah Dela Rosa C.','Hardware Malfunction','Main office, 1st floor','2022-05-01 21:30:00',13,'Low','Resolved','Printer produces faint or misaligned output.',NULL,'1. Check the physical printer display to see if there are any low toner or error warnings, and observe if a clear status message appears. 2. Print a test page directly from the printer menu to determine if the issue persists outside of the LAN connection, and observe the print quality. 3. If the print quality remains faint or misaligned, stop troubleshooting and contact IT Support for further assistance.','1. Verify the printer configuration and print density settings via the print server or local device management interface to check if toner conservation mode is enabled. 2. Inspect the physical print cartridge and rollers for toner depletion, debris, or wear that could cause faintness or misalignment. 3. Run printer calibration utilities to correct alignment issues and test output quality.',4875,0,NULL,13,'Michael Castillo',329,'Synthetic demo resolution: verified the affected device, applied the appropriate configuration or repair, and confirmed service with the reporter.','2022-05-01 17:30:00'),('INC-DEMO-0571','records application freezes while saving a form','Software / Application Error','[\"demo\",\"software-/-application-error\"]','LAN','2023-10-08 17:43:00','Public Affairs & Assistance Division[PAAD]','Synthetic training report: Application becomes unresponsive during routine record updates. This record is fictional and contains no real personal data.','Desktop Computer','Andres Flores N.','Software / Application Error','Main office, 2nd floor','2023-10-08 23:43:00',14,'Medium','Resolved','Records application freezes while saving a form.',NULL,'1. Wait a few moments to see if the application completes the save operation and recovers from the freeze. 2. If the application remains completely unresponsive, close the application window if possible or use Task Manager to end the application process. 3. Reopen the records application, log back in, and check if the record was saved or if it needs to be re-entered. 4. If the freezing persists every time you attempt to save, stop and contact IT Support for assistance.','1. Verify network connectivity and check switch port status for the LAN connection in Conference room A to rule out packet loss during the save action. 2. Review local event logs and application crash dumps on the desktop computer to identify any resource exhaustion or application fault signatures. 3. Check application server logs to determine if database locking, timeouts, or backend errors occurred concurrently with the user\'s save attempt.',4912,0,NULL,14,'Topher Villanueva',330,'Synthetic demo resolution: verified the affected device, applied the appropriate configuration or repair, and confirmed service with the reporter.','2023-10-08 19:43:00'),('INC-DEMO-0572','email client repeatedly requests sign-in','Email / Communication','[\"demo\",\"email